Commands 

1. Create StatefulSet

kubectl apply -f statefulset.yaml

2. Get StatefulSets

kubectl get statefulsets


3. Describe StatefulSet

kubectl describe statefulset <name>


4. Check Pods of StatefulSet

kubectl get pods

5. Scale StatefulSet

kubectl scale statefulset <name> --replicas=5

6. Delete StatefulSet

kubectl delete statefulset <name>

Important:

Pods are deleted in reverse order
Volumes (PVCs) are NOT deleted automatically

7. Delete with PVC Cleanup

kubectl delete pvc -l app=<label>

8. View Persistent Volume Claims (PVC)

kubectl get pvc


9. Logs of Specific Pod

kubectl logs nginx-0


10. Exec into Pod

kubectl exec -it nginx-0 -- /bin/bash


12. Restart StatefulSet Pods

kubectl rollout restart statefulset <name>



13. Check Rollout Status

kubectl rollout status statefulset <name>

14. Undo Rollout (if configured)

kubectl rollout undo statefulset <name>

15. Get Headless Service

kubectl get svc